# Build output. Fully regenerable from cards/ + facts/ with `npm run build`,
# so committing it would only create a second source of truth that can disagree
# with the first. git is the source of truth for cards/ and facts/.
dist/

# There are no dependencies to install — TypeScript runs directly on Node's
# native type stripping — so a lockfile or module tree here means something went
# wrong, and committing one would be worse.
node_modules/
package-lock.json

.DS_Store
*.log

# Rendered diagrams. The SVG is the source and it diffs; the PNG is derived from
# it by `rsvg-convert -w 2100 -o x.png x.svg`. Committing both would create a
# second artefact able to disagree with the first — the same reason dist/ is here.
docs/*.png

# Tier B scratch. `<CARD>.draft.json` is raw model output and `<CARD>.pr.md` is a
# pull-request body — an INPUT to a review and a message, neither a deliverable.
#
# The draft workflow used to `git add cards drafts`, so merging a draft PR carried
# both onto main permanently: one pair per redraft, forever, and a repository whose
# history fills up with the model's working notes. What a reviewer needs is the
# CARD diff; the artifact is how it got there, not what it is.
drafts/

# Kiro agent process artifacts (specs, session settings) — development
# tooling, not the deck itself. Kept locally, never published.
.kiro/
